- [x] I have searched [existing issues](https://github.com/facebook/yoga/issues) and this is not a duplicate

## Summary

- `roundLayoutResultsToPixelGrid`: position rounded from relative offset (`nodeTop`), size from absolute edges (`round(absoluteNodeBottom) - round(absoluteNodeTop)`).
- Parent on a fractional pixel → child pinned `bottom: 0` ends 1 px above parent's bottom.

## Repro

yoga-layout 3.2.1; `PixelGrid.cpp` on `main` rounds the same way.

```js
import Yoga, { Edge, PositionType } from "yoga-layout";

const config = Yoga.Config.create();
config.setPointScaleFactor(1);

const root = Yoga.Node.create(config);
root.setWidth(100);

const parent = Yoga.Node.create(config);
parent.setPositionType(PositionType.Absolute);
parent.setPosition(Edge.Top, 0.25);
parent.setWidth(100);
parent.setHeight(10.5);

const child = Yoga.Node.create(config);
child.setPositionType(PositionType.Absolute);
child.setPosition(Edge.Bottom, 0);
child.setWidth(100);
child.setHeight(10.25);

parent.insertChild(child, 0);
root.insertChild(parent, 0);
root.calculateLayout(undefined, undefined);

parent.getComputedLayout(); // { top: 0, height: 11 }
child.getComputedLayout();  // { top: 0, height: 10 } -> bottom 10, parent bottom 11
```

- Expected: child `top: 1, height: 10`, flush with parent bottom.
- Actual: 1 px gap.

## Why

- Child absolute edges 0.5 / 10.75 → rounded 1 / 11 → height 10.
- Position: `round(0.25) = 0`, not `round(0.5) - round(0.25) = 1`.

## Scale

- Scale 2.25 (Pixel 8 Pro), parent 506 tall at offset 0–4, `bottom: 0` child 150–260 tall: 2003 / 9176 layouts 1 px short.
- `top: 0; bottom: 0` child: 0 / 9176.
- Seen in React Native 0.88, Android: card shade `bottom: 0` stops 1 px above the card edge, image line shows.

## Related

- #1574: rounding is meant to avoid gaps between touching edges. This is one.

## Possible fix

- Non-text position: `round(absoluteNodeTop) - round(absoluteTop)` (same for left), reusing the rounded leading edge of the size.
- Text nodes keep floored relative position: absolute flooring drifts text 1 px per relayout.
- gentest reads positions with the same relative rounding (`Math.round(rect.top - parentTop)`); change it too. 2 generated expectations move.
- Draft PR: #2068.

Written with help from Claude (AI); reviewed and tested by me.

### Description

Since 15.16.0, web projects that bundle react-native-svg with Vite (rolldown) and react-native-web fail to build, and the dev server crashes during dependency optimization:

```
[MISSING_EXPORT] "TurboModuleRegistry" is not exported by "node_modules/react-native-web/dist/index.js".
   ╭─[ node_modules/react-native-svg/lib/module/fabric/NativeSvgSoundModule.js:1:10 ]
   │
 1 │ import { TurboModuleRegistry } from 'react-native';
   │          ─────────┬─────────
   │                   ╰─────────── Missing export
───╯
```

Cause: #3012 and #3016 added this to `src/lib/SvgTouchableMixin.ts` (around line 636):

```ts
if (Platform.OS === 'android' && !this.props.touchSoundDisabled) {
  const soundModule = require('../fabric/NativeSvgSoundModule').default;
  soundModule.playTouchSound();
}
```

`SvgTouchableMixin` is imported on web by `src/web/WebShape.ts`, so every web shape pulls it in. The `require()` sits behind a runtime `Platform.OS` check, but bundlers still resolve it statically. `lib/module` is ESM, and rolldown follows the inline `require()` into `NativeSvgSoundModule`, which imports `TurboModuleRegistry`. react-native-web does not export it. The same project builds and renders fine with 15.15.5.

Expected: `<Svg><Circle /></Svg>` builds and renders on web, as in 15.15.5.
Actual: `vite build` fails with the error above, and `vite` (dev) exits with `Error during dependency optimization: ... [MISSING_EXPORT] "TurboModuleRegistry"`.

Suggested fix: keep the native module out of the web module graph with a platform file outside `src/fabric` (so codegen does not see it), for example:

```ts
// src/lib/playTouchSound.ts
import { Platform } from 'react-native';
export function playTouchSound() {
  if (Platform.OS === 'android') {
    require('../fabric/NativeSvgSoundModule').default.playTouchSound();
  }
}

// src/lib/playTouchSound.web.ts
export function playTouchSound() {}
```

Then call `playTouchSound()` from `SvgTouchableMixin` when `!this.props.touchSoundDisabled`. I checked locally that a web-only no-op for this module is enough for the build to pass and the SVG to render.

Current workaround (Vite plugin that stubs the module):

```js
const STUB = '\0rnsvg-sound-stub';
const stubSoundModule = {
  name: 'stub-rnsvg-sound-module',
  enforce: 'pre',
  resolveId(id) { if (id.endsWith('/NativeSvgSoundModule')) return STUB; },
  load(id) { if (id === STUB) return 'export default { playTouchSound() {} };'; },
};
```

### Steps to reproduce

1. Create the three files below (plus `index.html` with `<div id="root"></div><script type="module" src="/src/main.jsx"></script>`).
2. `npm install`
3. `npm run build`: fails with the error above.
4. Change `react-native-svg` to `15.15.5`, `npm install`, `npm run build`: builds, and the circle renders in the browser.

`package.json`
```json
{
  "name": "rnsvg-web-vite-repro",
  "private": true,
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": { "dev": "vite", "build": "vite build", "preview": "vite preview" },
  "dependencies": {
    "@react-native/assets-registry": "0.88.0",
    "react": "19.3.1",
    "react-dom": "19.3.1",
    "react-native-svg": "15.16.0",
    "react-native-web": "0.21.4"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@vitejs/plugin-react": "6.1.2",
    "vite": "8.3.4"
  }
}
```
(`@react-native/assets-registry` is only there to get past a separate, older problem, which I am reporting separately.)

`vite.config.js`
```js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  resolve: {
    alias: { 'react-native': 'react-native-web' },
    extensions: ['.web.tsx', '.web.ts', '.web.jsx', '.web.js', '.tsx', '.ts', '.jsx', '.js', '.mjs', '.json'],
  },
});
```

`src/main.jsx`
```jsx
import { createRoot } from 'react-dom/client';
import Svg, { Circle } from 'react-native-svg';

createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(
  <Svg width={100} height={100}>
    <Circle cx={50} cy={50} r={40} fill="tomato" />
  </Svg>
);
```

### Snack or a link to a repository

The full reproduction is inline above (three small files). It is web-only, so a Snack does not apply.

### SVG version

15.16.0 (works in 15.15.5)

### React Native version

react-native-web 0.21.4 (react-native 0.88.0 installed as the peer dependency)

### Platforms

Web

### JavaScript runtime

V8 (Chrome)

### Workflow

Other: Vite 8.3.4 (rolldown 1.2.14) + react-native-web, no Metro or Expo.

### Architecture

N/A (web)

### Build type

Production bundle (`vite build`); the dev server fails too.

### Device

N/A (desktop browser). Node 26.12.0, npm 11.20.0, macOS.

### Reproduction link or steps

https://github.com/Pduhard/repro-rolldown-lost-side-effect (`npm install && node repro.mjs`)

```json
// lib/package.json
{ "sideEffects": ["./src/polyfill/*.js"] }
```

```js
// lib/src/polyfill/index.js
globalThis.expo = { EventEmitter: class EventEmitter {} };
```

```js
// lib/src/ensure.js
import './polyfill/index.js';
export function ensure() {}
```

```js
// lib/src/emitter.js
import { ensure } from './ensure.js';
ensure();
export const EventEmitter = globalThis.expo.EventEmitter;
```

### What is expected?

The polyfill runs before `emitter.js` reads it (webpack 5 and esbuild keep it).

### What is actually happening?

- `ensure()` is dropped as side-effect-free → `ensure.js` is unused → dropped, with the polyfill.
- `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'EventEmitter')`
- Real case: `expo-modules-core` on web (`EventEmitter.ts` → `ensureNativeModulesAreInstalled.ts` → `polyfill/index.web.ts`), through Vite's dep optimizer.

### System Info

```Shell
rolldown 1.2.14 (fails since 1.0.0-rc.17), Node 24.17.0, Linux x64
```

### Any additional comments?

- Hit in the Vitest browser-mode tests of a React Native Web app: Vite's dep optimizer bundles `expo-modules-core`, whose `EventEmitter.ts` calls `ensureNativeModulesAreInstalled()` to load `polyfill/index.web.ts`, and every test file fails on import.
- Unlike #11079, webpack 5 keeps the polyfill here; only Rollup drops it.

Investigated and written with Claude Code; I reviewed it.

